Still I would have to make a choice whether I would be willing to run 
the risks of the penalties that come with making that choice.  My 
argument goes in the direction of increasing the number of possible 
choices and of game variability, not in the direction of making choices 
artificially scarce.

>>It would also be a means for an already strong character to create
>>altars in a cinvenient place in order to avoid backtracking each time
>>to level 3 or even to the mines just in order sacrifice or to
>>identify the buc state of things.
