Sure, but that's not the point for me.  I do have the patience and I 
will most of the time choose the way that makes life safer for my 
character in the long run.  Nevertheless, I don't see why the game has 
to be made artificially boring.  If my character can avoid boredom by 
doing something complicated once that will provide the same result as a 
tedious repetitive alternative, then I consider a change of the game 
allowing the more interesting approach desirable.


